/* book exam traps: Multiplying the turns ratio by 12 V. The secondary voltage is n times the primary emf at the break, a few hundred volts. | Saying hot electrodes need more voltage. A hot surface frees electrons more easily, so the firing voltage falls; pressure and gap raise it. | A hot plug is not a plug for a hot engine. A hot plug suits a cool-running, lightly loaded engine; a cold plug suits a hot, high-power engine. | Mixing available voltage (what the coil can give) with required voltage (what the plug needs). The engine runs on the difference, the reserve. | Resistor plugs and suppressors cut radio noise; they add resistance in the secondary, not spark energy. */
